&gt; React feels natural because it never asks you to stop writing JavaScript<p>I want to increment some counter on the webpage. Which approach feels natural?<p><pre><code>  increment = () =&gt; {
    this.setState((prevState) =&gt; ({ count: prevState.count + 1 }));
  };

  const increment = () =&gt; setCount((count) =&gt; count + 1);

  function increment() {
    count += 1;
  }
</code></pre>
No one wakes up saying &quot;please let me mutate simple state with function calls&quot;.
